**[Suggestion]** The post step's best-effort error handling is tested here (`set -uo pipefail` and `continuing.`), but the finalize step's equivalent guards are not asserted — the finalize step also has `set -uo pipefail` and `|| echo "::warning::...continuing."`, but neither is asserted on `finalizeStatusCommentStep`. — Failure scenario: a future edit removes the `|| echo` fallback from the finalize step's `gh api --method PATCH` call; a transient API failure then fails the step, and since it runs under `always()` the entire job is marked failed even though the round succeeded.

```suggestion
    expect(postStatusCommentStep).toContain('set -uo pipefail');
    expect(postStatusCommentStep).toContain('continuing.');
    expect(finalizeStatusCommentStep).toContain('set -uo pipefail');
    expect(finalizeStatusCommentStep).toContain('continuing.');
```

